    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2F73gZiPLTE9XBjJJzDdqaE)_\n\nFollow-up to #408 / #412 (`sp-litnotes-meta-add-all-tables`).\n\n## Summary\n\n- An existing `* Sections` heading is reused (any level, tags allowed); the dblock goes at the start of its content, after a property drawer, with a blank line before and after.\n- A chapter table block never stays outside that heading: above the first heading, under another heading, or after text under Sections, it is moved on re-run.\n- Every table block is brought into the saved template format `#+BEGIN: collection-query-table :view \"NAME\"`:\n  - `vulpea-table` is renamed, other parameters stay.\n  - Parameters equal to a view become `:view NAME`.\n  - A block for the note itself (`:parent-of` self or its ID) gets the note's view; the old line shows in the preview.\n  - Blocks with `:view`, or for another note, are kept.\n- Idempotent: blocks already in place are not touched.\n- `C-u` preview lists \"Would be fixed\" with what would happen (heading added, table moved, header old and new); it writes nothing.\n- A real run copies each note to `sp-litnotes-meta-backup-directory/<time>/` before saving, and the summary links the folder.\n- `backfill-children` uses the same function.\n- Literate doc updated as bullets; ERT tests added (moves, reuse, migration, preview and backup). Tests were run with stubs on Emacs 29.3; 5 other tests in the file already failed on `main` in this container and still do.\n- No CHANGELOG edits.\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [x] Pull this branch, restart Emacs\n- [x] Dry run first: `C-u M-x sp-litnotes-meta-add-all-tables` and check the \"Would be fixed\" list (heading added, table moved, header migrated); no file changes, no backup folder (untested by Claude on the real vault)\n- [ ] Pick one note with a table under another heading and run `M-x sp-litnotes-meta-backfill-children` or the full command on it: block ends at the start of `* Sections`, blank lines around (untested by Claude)\n- [ ] Note with an existing `* Sections` heading with text: heading is reused, not duplicated, block sits before the text (untested by Claude)\n- [ ] Note with an old `#+BEGIN: vulpea-table ...` block: becomes `#+BEGIN: collection-query-table :view \"...\"` (untested by Claude)\n- [ ] Full run `M-x sp-litnotes-meta-add-all-tables`: the summary links the backup folder, and a changed note is there in its old form (untested by Claude)\n- [ ] Run it again: nothing changed, no new backup folder (untested by Claude)\n- [ ] Edge: a block with `:view` plus an override (e.g. `:sort-by`) or a `:parent-of` of another note stays unchanged (untested by Claude)\n- [ ] Regression: `M-x sp-litnotes-meta-refresh-all-tables` and `M-x sp-org-dblock-insert-template` still work (untested by Claude)\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiBTiyvqBK7wpEnNo5c)_",
